A vast underground catacomb viewed from a dramatic low angle, rendered in Vincent van Gogh's swirling, expressive brushwork style. Ancient stone alcoves line the walls, but instead of bones, they hold glowing crystalline data cubes and rolled digital scrolls emanating soft blue and amber light. Thick impasto strokes create turbulent energy in the shadows between alcoves. In the center, a single ornate sarcophagus made of circuit-board patterns and copper filigree sits open, revealing layers of nested containers within containers, each smaller one glowing brighter than the last. Swirling starry-night-style energy spirals upward from the deepest container toward a vaulted ceiling. The color palette features deep prussian blues, warm yellows, and oxidized copper greens. Cobwebs made of fine golden data streams connect the alcoves. The atmosphere is reverent yet technological, treating forgotten digital artifacts as sacred relics deserving proper eternal rest.
